{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n\\n/*\\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\\n */\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\n/*\\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\\n */\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n\\n  return bodies;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\\n */\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n  int nbodies;\\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n  size_t count = (size_t)nbodies;\\n  float *state = (float *)malloc(6 * count * sizeof(float));\\n  float *restrict x = state;\\n  float *restrict y = x + count;\\n  float *restrict z = y + count;\\n  float *restrict vx = z + count;\\n  float *restrict vy = vx + count;\\n  float *restrict vz = vy + count;\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n    x[i] = bodies[i].x;\\n    y[i] = bodies[i].y;\\n    z[i] = bodies[i].z;\\n    vx[i] = bodies[i].vx;\\n    vy[i] = bodies[i].vy;\\n    vz[i] = bodies[i].vz;\\n  }\\n\\n  /*\\n   * Each force destination writes only its own velocity components.  The\\n   * scalar accumulation order over j is retained, while position and\\n   * velocity streams are independent, unit-stride arrays.\\n   */\\n#pragma omp parallel default(none) shared(x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, nbodies)\\n  {\\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n        const float xi = x[i];\\n        const float yi = y[i];\\n        const float zi = z[i];\\n        float fx = 0.0f;\\n        float fy = 0.0f;\\n        float fz = 0.0f;\\n\\n        for (int j = 0; j < nbodies; j++) {\\n          float dx = x[j] - xi;\\n          float dy = y[j] - yi;\\n          float dz = z[j] - zi;\\n          float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n          float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n          float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n          fx += dx * inv_dist3;\\n          fy += dy * inv_dist3;\\n          fz += dz * inv_dist3;\\n        }\\n\\n        vx[i] += DT*fx;\\n        vy[i] += DT*fy;\\n        vz[i] += DT*fz;\\n      }\\n\\n#pragma omp for simd schedule(static)\\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\\n        x[i] += vx[i] * DT;\\n        y[i] += vy[i] * DT;\\n        z[i] += vz[i] * DT;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\\n    bodies[i].x = x[i];\\n    bodies[i].y = y[i];\\n    bodies[i].z = z[i];\\n    bodies[i].vx = vx[i];\\n    bodies[i].vy = vy[i];\\n    bodies[i].vz = vz[i];\\n  }\\n\\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\\n\\n  free(state);\\n  free(bodies);\\n\\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/nbody.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Separating body fields into non-overlapping unit-stride streams improves the hot force loop's memory access and makes the independent integration loop legally SIMD-vectorizable, while retaining the original per-body j-order of floating-point force accumulation.\",\"notes\":\"The force phase retains its original arithmetic expressions and serial accumulation order for every destination body; barriers continue to separate force and position phases.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Deinterleave the input AoS body representation into six contiguous position and velocity arrays for simulation, then reinterleave only for binary output.\",\"Hoist each force destination position into scalar loop invariants while preserving the original inner-loop order and accumulation sequence.\",\"Use OpenMP for-simd only on the independent position-update loop.\"]}"}}
